            <ArticleTitle>Central modulation of pain perception.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-13</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The information presented in this article provides a basis for individual variability in the sensation of pain and the behavioral correlates associated with pain. The knowledge of pain-inhibitory and pain-facilitating pathways linked to cognitive, emotional, and stress-response systems leads to a greater understanding of the complexities of the experience of pain. Appreciation of the influence of these higher centers should lead to improvements in the clinical management of pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
